  why: 'Stories are older than writing; epics like Gilgamesh and Homer were sung before they were written. Literature preserves what it felt like to be human in other times, and it trains the reader to understand other minds, arguments and the uses of language.',
  qs: ['Why do humans tell stories?', 'What makes a book last for centuries?', 'How do novels change politics (Uncle Tom’s Cabin, 1984)?', 'How should we read works with values we reject?'],
